# Task 144-021: Test — heartbeat-daemon + mid-sprint-adapter + ci-reporter (+24 test)

## Baseline
- heartbeat-daemon.test.ts: 14 tests (validateCommand only — no async function tests)
- ci-reporter.test.ts: 7 tests (appendCiHealthToRetro, appendCiLearningsToMemory — no formatCiHealthSection, readCiReportTrend, runCiLearningAnalysis)
- mid-sprint-adapter.test.ts: 0 tests (does not exist)

## Plan

### heartbeat-daemon.test.ts (+10 tests)
1. runHeartbeat — executes pending tasks, skips done tasks
2. runHeartbeat — creates HEARTBEAT.md when missing
3. runHeartbeat — logs results to heartbeat-log.md
4. runHeartbeat — handles command validation failure (blocked command)
5. HeartbeatDaemon — start() runs first heartbeat, sets interval
6. HeartbeatDaemon — stop() clears interval, removes PID
7. HeartbeatDaemon — running property reflects timer state
8. readDaemonPid — returns null for non-existent PID file
9. readDaemonPid — returns null for NaN PID content
10. stopDaemonByPid — returns false when no PID file

### mid-sprint-adapter.test.ts (+10 tests, new file)
1. shouldReroute — returns false for DONE task
2. shouldReroute — returns false when NO_GO but max reroutes reached
3. shouldReroute — returns false when GO_WITH_TECH_DEBT and reroute_on_tech_debt=false
4. shouldReroute — returns true for NO_GO with alternative routing
5. shouldReroute — returns false when alternative is same as original
6. shouldReroute — increments reroute count and sets routingMeta
7. applyReroute — mutates task with new decision
8. suggestReroute — excludes failed agent/skills
9. suggestReroute — returns null on routing error
10. shouldReroute — respects confidence threshold

### ci-reporter.test.ts (+8 tests)
1. formatCiHealthSection — returns empty array for null report
2. formatCiHealthSection — formats positive coverage delta
3. formatCiHealthSection — formats negative coverage delta
4. formatCiHealthSection — singular/plural regression label
5. readCiReportTrend — returns stable when no reports
6. readCiReportTrend — detects increasing test count trend
7. readCiReportTrend — detects decreasing coverage trend
8. readCiReportTrend — limits to maxSprints

Total: +28 new tests (≥24 target)

